Some important Interview Questions (beginner level) on shell scripting.

 Disk usage is high on a server. How do you find large files?
du -ah / | sort -rh | head -10
 Used to identify space-consuming files in production servers.

How do you find and delete files older than 30 days?
find /var/log -type f -mtime +30 -delete
 Commonly used for log cleanup automation.

 A service is down. How will you check and restart it using a script?
systemctl status nginx
systemctl restart nginx
Used in monitoring and self-healing scripts.

 How do you check if a process is running?
ps -ef | grep nginx
or
pgrep nginx

 How do you monitor CPU and memory usage?
top
free -m
Often automated and combined with alerting scripts.

You need to take a backup of a directory daily. How?
tar -czvf backup.tar.gz /app/data
 Scheduled using cron jobs.

How do you schedule a script to run every day at midnight?
0 0 * * * /path/script.sh
 Very common cron interview question.

 A script should stop execution if any command fails. How?
set -e
 Helps avoid partial failures in automation.

 How do you pass arguments to a shell script?
./script.sh dev frontend
Inside script:
echo $1
echo $2

 How do you check return status of a command?
echo $?
 Used to validate success or failure in scripts.

 How do you check open ports on a server?
netstat -tulnp
or
ss -tulnp

 How do you automate log rotation?
 Using:
logrotate
Shell scripts + cron
